assistant: Subject: Convert cent prices from vendor API 2026-10-01 to dollars

Starting with API version 2026-10-01, the vendor returns `price` in cents instead of dollars. In the recorded call, every laptop came back at exactly 100× its v1 price (1199 became 119900), with the same products and stock. The published spec only says "Unit price", so it never stated the unit. `search_products` passed `price` through unchanged, so it reported cent values as US dollars. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides prices by 100 when it is 2026-10-01 or later; older versions keep a divisor of 1, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output as before. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, but `test/traces/` is empty, so no test replays the new-version call yet. `get_product` reads the same price field and probably needs the same fix, but I had no 2026-10-01 recording for it, so I left it unchanged.

